@vsm 1.0
// opsroom_capability_audit.vsm — FUNCTIONAL evaluation of the opsroom (no design considerations).
// author: Fable [O] 2026-07-04. Question: can our opsroom operate across ALL the layers of complexity
// the original Cybersyn opsroom was built for? Benchmark = Beer's opsroom FUNCTIONS, not its looks.

audit(OPSROOM_CAPABILITY) {

  frame:
    "An opsroom is not a dashboard — it is the room from which a viable system is OPERATED. Beer's design
     had to enable FIVE operations, at EVERY VSM level (S1-S5) and EVERY recursion level (L3→L2→L1):
       SENSE     — see the real state of each level.
       ALERT     — be drawn to what is off-normal (algedonic, management-by-exception).
       ANTICIPATE— simulate/project futures (S4; Cybersyn's CHECO simulator).
       DECIDE    — act FROM the room (the armchair buttons; low-variety human input).
       AUDIT     — see what happened, attributably.
     Our opsroom is a strong SENSING surface for the nucleus. Measured against all five × all levels, it is
     still a DISPLAY, not yet a control ROOM. The gaps below are the requirements not yet considered."

  // ── THE MATRIX — have / partial / missing ─────────────────────────────────────
  // legend: ✓ have · ◐ partial · ✗ missing
  sense: {
    S1_operations:  "◐ nucleus state (cybernetic-rag) yes; the S1 FLEET (clima 80 stations, econ) NOT as first-class operational views",
    S2_coordination:"✗ NO coordination view — anti-oscillation / inter-unit conflict is invisible",
    S3_control:     "◐ s3-viz shows resource grants; the full here-and-now control picture is thin",
    S3star_audit:   "◐ system-topology shows 'recent algedonic activity'; no dedicated audit view",
    S4_intelligence:"✗ NO environment scan, NO forecaster surfaced (it runs in the backend, invisible in the room)",
    S5_policy:      "✗ NO policy/identity view; the covenant, the ends, the ceiling — not represented",
  }
  alert:      "◐ the R/Y/G algedonic triage EXISTS as a one-off artifact + partial in system-topology; NOT a
               live first-class management-by-exception panel (the single strongest Cybersyn correspondence, unbuilt)",
  anticipate: "✗ THE BIGGEST GAP. Cybersyn had CHECO — a simulator to run 'what-if' futures. We have the
               Markov forecaster in the backend but it is NOT in the room and NOT interactive. You cannot
               PLAN or anticipate from the opsroom today — only watch the present.",
  decide:     "✗ view-only. The original opsroom was a DECISION space (the armchair buttons). We have NO
               decision surface and NO human input path. supervision_layer.spec.vsm designs this but it is
               unbuilt — and it must cover more than escalations (see gaps).",
  audit:      "◐ the audit chain (vsf.alpha.s3star.audit) + attributable signing exist by design; there is
               NO accountability VIEW — you cannot, from the room, see the shape of what the machine did.",

  // ── VSF-SPECIFIC REQUIREMENTS — beyond Cybersyn (Beer could not do these) ──────
  beyond_cybersyn: {
    calibration_state: "✗ which instruments are CALIBRATED (Axis-1) — the meta-viability layer. Cybersyn
                        assumed its gauges; we PROVED ours discriminate. The room should show gauge health.",
    attestation_trust:"✗ is each node covenant-compliant, calibrated, ATTESTED (beacon/EVC)? The trust state
                        of the recursive network is invisible.",
    autonomy_state:   "◐ s3-viz shows grants; but WHICH loops are running autonomously vs holding-for-human
                       (Axis-2 loop1/loop2 + escalations) is not framed as an operability view.",
  }

  // ── THE GAPS, PRIORITISED (what to ADDRESS) ───────────────────────────────────
  gaps_ranked: [
    "G1 DECIDE — a decision surface (the room must let rmw3 ACT, not just watch). supervision_layer is the
        seed; widen it: escalations + policy adjustment + the low-variety input path. [backend: DS · front: specialist]",
    "G2 ANTICIPATE — surface the forecaster as an interactive S4/CHECO view: project futures, run what-ifs,
        see p(excursion) per node. The room without anticipation cannot govern strategically. [DS + specialist]",
    "G3 ALERT — the live algedonic management-by-exception panel (R/Y/G by subsystem, from the ledger). [DS + specialist]",
    "G4 SENSE the missing levels — S2 coordination view, S5 policy/identity view, and the S1 FLEET (recursion). [DS + specialist]",
    "G5 RECURSION NAVIGATION — descend L3→L2→L1 (nucleus → S1 → its sub-units). Beer's recursion made operable. [specialist]",
    "G6 AUDIT view — the accountability surface (shape of autonomous action; attributable). Pairs with G1. [DS + specialist]",
    "G7 META-VIABILITY — calibration + attestation + autonomy state (the VSF-specific layers). [DS + specialist]",
    "G8 TEMPORAL DEPTH — trend/trajectory ('is the whole system improving?'), not just NOW + dL. [DS + specialist]",
  ]

  data_availability_note:
    "Most gaps are already FEED-READY — the data exists, only the view is missing: forecaster (s4_markov_projection.json),
     algedonic ledger (LXC 104), audit chain (vsf.alpha.s3star.audit), S1 φ↑ (clima/econ logs), peripheral_health,
     calibration census. G1/G6 need supervision_layer's new streams (vsf.alpha.s5.decision). So the lift is mostly
     VIEW-side (specialist) + a few backend feeds (DS) — NOT new instrumentation."

  verdict:
    "Our opsroom is an excellent SENSING surface for the nucleus and a real S3 resource view. To operate
     'across all layers' like Beer's, it needs to become a control ROOM: add ANTICIPATION (S4/CHECO), a
     DECISION surface (S5/action), the missing SENSE levels (S2, S5, the fleet), recursion navigation, and
     the VSF meta-layers (calibration/attestation/autonomy). Almost all of it is feed-ready — the gap is
     views, not data. Priority order = DECIDE + ANTICIPATE first (they turn a display into a room)."

  owner: "Fable [O] (this audit). Backends → DS [S] (the missing feeds). Views → UX/UI specialist (per
          docs/design/interface_brief.md). rmw3 (S5): confirm the priority (G1/G2 first?)."
  status: "AUDIT complete — 8 gaps ranked. The opsroom is a display today; the gaps are what make it a control room."
}
